n and eosin staining <bold>(C,D)</bold> of the growth plate at postnatal day 36 in a C57BL/6 mouse. Magnified images <bold>(B,D)</bold> denote cellular swelling and size variation of hypertrophic chondrocytes as they move towards the primary spongiosa. RZ: resting zone, PZ: proliferating zone, PHZ: pre-hypertrophic zone, HZ: hypertrophic zone, PS: primary spongiosa. Scale bars: 100 μM.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" position=\"float\" orientation=\"portrait\" xlink:href=\"nihms-1734042-f0002.jpg\"/></fig></floats-group></article></pmc-articleset>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
