ology_prefix\":\"UBERON\",\"short_form\":\"CL_1000217\",\"description\":[\"Any chondrocyte that is part of some growth plate cartilage.\"],\"label\":\"growth plate cartilage chondrocyte\",\"obo_id\":\"CL:1000217\",\"type\":\"class\"},{\"iri\":\"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0003417\",\"ontology_name\":\"uberon\",\"ontology_prefix\":\"UBERON\",\"short_form\":\"GO_0003417\",\"description\":[\"The process whose specific outcome is the progression of the cartilage that will provide a scaffold for mineralization of endochondral bones as they elongate or grow.\"],\"label\":\"growth plate cartilage development\",\"obo_id\":\"GO:0003417\",\"type\":\"class\"},{\"iri\":\"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0003422\",\"ontology_name\":\"uberon\",\"ontology_prefix\":\"UBERON\",\"short_form\":\"GO_0003422\",\"description\":[\"The process in which the anatomical structures of growth plate cartilage are generated and organized.\"],\"label\":\"growth plate cartilage morphogenesis\",\"obo_id\":\"GO:0003422\",\"type\":\"class\"},{\"iri\":\"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0003054\",\"ontology_name\":\"uberon\",\"related_synonyms\":[\"alar plate\",\"future brain roof plate\"],\"ontology_prefix\":\"UBERON\",\"short_form\":\"UBERON_0003054\",\"description\":[\"A single row of glia at the dorsal midline of the developing neural tube along the entire anterior-posterior axis. This region provides inductive signals for the specification of neuronal cell types and of the specification of neural crest cells. The cells comprising the roof plate are the precursors to radial glial cells.\"],\"label\":\"roof plate\",\"obo_id\":\"UBERON:0003054\",\"type\":\"class\",\"exact_synonyms\":[\"roofplate\",\"roof plate neural tube region\",\"roof plate neural tube\"]},{\"iri\":\"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0003063\",\"ontology_name\":\"uberon\",\"ontology_prefix\":\"UBERON\",\"short_form\":\"UBERON_0003063\",\"broad_synonyms\":[\"head mesenchyme\",\"head mesoderm\"],\"description\":[\"A horseshoe-shaped thickening of the endoderm at the cranial (rostral) end of the primitive streak formed by the involution of Spemann\\u0027s organizer cells which, together with the notochord, induces the formation of the neural plate from the overlying ectodermal cells and contributes mesodermal type cells to the surrounding tissue.\"],\"label\":\"prechordal plate\",\"obo_id\":\"UBERON:0003063\",\"type\":\"class\"},{\"iri\":\"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0003075\",\"ontology_name\":\"uberon\",\"related_synonyms\":[\"presumptive central nervous system\",\"lamina neuralis\"],\"ontology_prefix\":\"UBERON\",\"short_form\":\"UBERON_0003075\",\"description\":[\"A region of embryonic ectodermal cells that lie directly above the notochord. During neurulation, they change shape and produce an infolding of the neural plate (the neural fold) that then seals to form the neural tube[XAO]. The earliest recognizable dorsal ectodermal primordium of the central nervous system present near the end of gastrulation before infolding to form the neural keel; consists of a thickened pseudostratified epithelium[ZFA].\"],\"label\":\"neural plate\",\"obo_id\":\"UBERON:0003075\",\"type\":\"class\"},{\"iri\":\"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0003079\",\"ontology_name\":\"uberon\",\"related_synonyms\":[\"FP\",\"bodenplatte\",\"ventral plate\"],\"ontology_prefix\":\"UBERON\",\"short_form\":\"UBERON_0003079\",\"description\":[\"The specialized glial structure (non-neuronal cells) situated at the ventral midline of the embryonic neural tube; this structure spans the anteroposterior axis from the midbrain to the tail regions, separating the left and right basal plates of the developing neural tube, and serves as an organizer to ventralize tissues in the embryo as well as to guide neuronal positioning and differentiation along the dorsoventral axis of the neural tube.\",\"\\\"A structure integral to the developing nervous system of vertebrate organisms. Located on the ventral midline of the embryonic neural tube, the floor plate is a specialized glial structure that spans the anteroposterior axis from the midbrain to the tail regions. It has been shown that the floor plate is conserved among vertebrates with homologous structures in invertebrates such as the fruit fly Drosophila and the nematode C. elegans. Functionally, the structure serves as an organizer to ventralize tissues in the embryo as well as to guide neuronal positioning and differentiation along the dorsoventral axis of the neural tube.\\\"\"],\"label\":\"floor plate\",\"obo_id\":\"UBERON:0003079\",\"type\":\"class\",\"exact_synonyms\":[\"floorplate\"]}],\"numFound\":620,\"start\":0},\"responseHeader\":{\"QTime\":41,\"status\":0},\"facet_counts\":{\"facet_fields\":{\"ontologyPreferredPrefix\":[\"UBERON\",\"620\",\"ADDICTO\",\"0\",\"ADO\",\"0\",\"AEO\",\"0\",\"AFO\",\"0\",\"AGRO\",\"0\",\"AISM\",\"0\",\"AMPHX\",\"0\",\"APO\",\"0\",\"APOLLO_SV\",\"0\",\"ARO\",\"0\",\"AfPO\",\"0\",\"BAO\",\"0\",\"BCIO\",\"0\",\"BCO\",\"0\",\"BFO\",\"0\",\"BMONT\",\"0\",\"BSPO\",\"0\",\"BTO\",\"0\",\"CAO\",\"0\",\"CARO\",\"0\",\"CCF\",\"0\",\"CCO\",\"0\",\"CDAO\",\"0\",\"CDNO\",\"0\",\"CHEBI\",\"0\",\"CHEMINF\",\"0\",\"CHIRO\",\"0\",\"CHMO\",\"0\",\"CIDO\",\"0\",\"CIO\",\"0\",\"CL\",\"0\",\"CLAO\",\"0\",\"CLO\",\"0\",\"CLYH\",\"0\",\"CMO\",\"0\",\"CMPO\",\"0\",\"COB\",\"0\",\"COLAO\",\"0\",\"COVOC\",\"0\",\"CPONT\",\"0\",\"CRO\",\"0\",\"CTENO\",\"0\",\"CVDO\",\"0\",\"DDANAT\",\"0\",\"DDPHENO\",\"0\",\"DHBA\",\"0\",\"DIDEO\",\"0\",\"DISDRIV\",\"0\",\"DMBA\",\"0\",\"DOID\",\"0\",\"DRON\",\"0\",\"DUO\",\"0\",\"EC\",\"0\",\"ECAO\",\"0\",\"ECO\",\"0\",\"ECOCORE\",\"0\",\"ECTO\",\"0\",\"EDAM\",\"0\",\"EFO\",\"0\",\"EMAPA\",\"0\",\"EMI\",\"0\",\"ENM\",\"0\",\"ENSGLOSS\",\"0\",\"ENVO\",\"0\",\"EPIO\",\"0\",\"EUPATH\",\"0\",\"EXMO\",\"0\",\"ExO\",\"0\",\"FAO\",\"0\",\"FBbi\",\"0\",\"FBbt\",\"0\",\"FBcv\",\"0\",\"FBdv\",\"0\",\"FIDEO\",\"0\",\"FLOPO\",\"0\",\"FMA\",\"0\",\"FOBI\",\"0\",\"FOODON\",\"0\",\"FOVT\",\